    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds a production-oriented wallet cash-out lifecycle after transparent platform-fee settlement.\n\n### Backend\n- reserves wallet funds atomically when a payout is requested\n- requires an ACTIVE account and current VERIFIED identity\n- persists an auditable payout lifecycle and immutable events via Flyway V39\n- uses stable provider idempotency keys across retries\n- restores funds only after a definite failure, explicit queued cancellation, or audited admin decline\n- moves ambiguous provider outcomes to REVIEW_REQUIRED instead of risking double payout\n- rechecks account/KYC safety before dispatch\n- production provider defaults to disabled; sandbox is explicitly local/CI-only\n- private user eligibility/history/cancel endpoints plus admin review/audit endpoints\n\n### Web\n- adds payout eligibility, amount entry, history and cancellation directly to Wallet\n- links unverified users to identity verification\n- clearly labels sandbox as test-only and never presents it as a real bank transfer\n- surfaces PAYOUT_RESERVE / PAYOUT_RESTORE in wallet ledger history\n\n### Accounting semantics\n- available wallet balance is fungible; escrow refunds can be reused or cashed out after KYC\n- requesting payout immediately removes the amount from spendable balance\n- successful PAID payout does not debit again because reservation already did it\n- cancelled/definitively failed payout restores the reserved amount idempotently\n\n### Testing / operations\n- dedicated Worker payout smoke verifies KYC gate, reservation, idempotency, cancellation+restore and sandbox PAID lifecycle against PostgreSQL\n- docs/PAYOUTS.md documents state machine, privacy, provider boundary and relation to the upcoming publish-with-payment flow\n\n## Safety\nNo real payout provider is enabled by this PR. `sandbox` never sends money and production should keep `PAYOUT_PROVIDER=disabled` until a live regulated provider adapter and recipient onboarding are configured.\n\nDo not merge until every latest-head check is green.",
